<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_SheenExposureLock.xml            UtinniPatches - ROT_SHEEN_WEATHER_1 build pass

  rot_kit_spec.md M1 ("The Sheen"), ticket 2: "reuse RC4 as a permanent
  condition (RUT_SheenExposureLock, attached via the BiomeDef's own
  <biomeMapConditions>, exactly the shipped RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock.xml shape -
  pure XML, no weather forcing, no damage fields)." Shape copied directly
  from that file (GameConditionDefs/RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock.xml).

  No forcedWeather: unlike Miasma (which forces one permanent haze), the Rot
  keeps a natural weather ROTATION between Clear/DryThunderstorm and the
  three reskinned Sheen weathers (RUT_TheRot.xml's own
  baseWeatherCommonalities) - the exposure clock is meant to pause between
  Sheen-falls, not run every tick.

  No damageDef/hediffToApply set, same as Miasma's own "no damage fields":
  this condition's only job is to bootstrap RUT_SheenCoating onto every
  eligible pawn on the map (carrierHediff/carrierHediffSeverity,
  EnsureCarrierHediff in GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather.cs - NOT gated
  by onlyUnroofed, so a roofed pawn also carries the hediff and its own comp
  can decay it via severityPerDayUnexposed). RUT_SheenCoating's own comp
  (HediffCompProperties_SheenExposure, RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards -
  RUT_RotSporeKit_SheenHediffs.xml) does the actual weather-gated,
  gear-slowed, symbiont-immune severity math - the "verify
  EnvironmentalWeatherExtension can gate on current weather" question the
  ticket raised is answered by putting that gate on the HEDIFF's own comp
  (RM_HediffComp_EnvironmentalExposure already supports onlyDuringWeather;
  this pass widens it to a weather LIST additively, same file, no behaviour
  change for RUT_MiasmaExposure's existing single-weather config) rather
  than on this shared GameCondition class, which stays untouched.

  damageIntervalTicks 2500 (~1 in-game hour) matches RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock's
  own bootstrap cadence exactly - carried over, not re-invented.

  MayRequire is load-bearing: conditionClass/modExtension Class live in
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards; carrierHediff (RUT_SheenCoating) is a
  RotSporeKit def, mandrake.rut.rotsporekit.
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards,mandrake.rut.rotsporekit">
    <defName>RUT_SheenExposureLock</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather</conditionClass>
    <label>the Sheen's breath</label>
    <description>The Rot's own reproductive cycle never truly pauses here — even between Sheen-falls, its spores hang thin in the air, ready to seed anyone who lingers unroofed too long.</description>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <allowUnderground>false</allowUnderground>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.EnvironmentalWeatherExtension">
        <carrierHediff>RUT_SheenCoating</carrierHediff>
        <carrierHediffSeverity>0.0001</carrierHediffSeverity>
        <damageIntervalTicks>2500</damageIntervalTicks>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
